WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.670
<v Examiner>Stimulant, or depressant?

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.778
<v Examiner>What's the difference?

3
00:00:04.228 --> 00:00:07.373
Pusheen is on these slides, so this is the concept.

4
00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:11.936
Stimulants and depressants are the two main groups of mind-altering drugs,

5
00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:15.636
and they act in opposite ways on the central nervous system.

6
00:00:15.636 --> 00:00:18.843
Stimulants, uppers, speed up the body and the brain.

7
00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:23.961
Depressants, downers, slow them down, so they calm, sedate, and make people drowsy.

8
00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:25.374
On her chart.

9
00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:28.189
Stimulants: MDMA, and methamphetamine.

10
00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:34.410
Depressants: alcohol, GHB, sedatives such as lorazepam and zopiclone, nitrous oxide,

11
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.373
and inhalants like glue, gas and petrol.

12
00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:42.188
Both stimulant and depressant: nicotine, marijuana, psychedelics,

13
00:00:42.188 --> 00:00:44.187
and synthetic cannabinoids.

14
00:00:44.637 --> 00:00:45.802
Why a nurse cares.

15
00:00:45.802 --> 00:00:49.878
Two depressants together slow breathing more than either alone.

16
00:00:49.878 --> 00:00:55.248
That's why mixing alcohol with an opioid, or with benzodiazepines, is so dangerous.

17
00:00:55.248 --> 00:00:58.419
You'll hear that again in the interactions track.

18
00:00:58.869 --> 00:01:03.452
She also showed slang on Pusheen slides, so it's not for marks,

19
00:01:03.452 --> 00:01:05.490
but it's useful on the ward.

20
00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.018
P is methamphetamine.

21
00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:08.837
Four twenty is marijuana.

22
00:01:08.837 --> 00:01:11.238
Lean is codeine in a fizzy drink.

23
00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:12.693
Pingers are ecstasy.

24
00:01:12.693 --> 00:01:13.857
Fishies are GHB.

25
00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:15.603
Nangs are nitrous oxide.

26
00:01:15.603 --> 00:01:16.767
And acid is LSD.

27
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:17.771
<v Examiner>Once more.

28
00:01:17.771 --> 00:01:19.265
<v Examiner>Stimulants and depressants.

29
00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:26.136
Stimulants speed up the body and brain: MDMA, methamphetamine.

30
00:01:26.136 --> 00:01:31.698
Depressants slow them down: alcohol, GHB, sedatives, nitrous oxide, inhalants.

31
00:01:31.698 --> 00:01:36.904
Some are both: nicotine, marijuana, psychedelics, synthetic cannabinoids.

32
00:01:36.904 --> 00:01:42.323
Two depressants together, like alcohol and an opioid, are the dangerous mix.
